.TH KTX_CREATE 1 "2026-10-27" "ktx (Rust port)" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
ktx_create \- create a KTX2 file from input images
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ktx
create [OPTION...] <input\-file...> <output\-file>
.SH DESCRIPTION
Builds a KTX2 texture of the format given by
.B \-\-format
from PNG, JPEG or EXR images, or from raw data with
.BR \-\-raw .
Input images are assigned in order to levels, layers, faces and depth slices. The result can be
resized, mipmapped, color converted, encoded and supercompressed in the same step.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-format <vkformat>
Vulkan format of the texture data, e.g. R8G8B8A8_SRGB (required).
.TP
.B \-\-cubemap, \-\-1d, \-\-layers <n>, \-\-depth <n>
Texture type and dimensions.
.TP
.B \-\-generate\-mipmap, \-\-levels <n>
Generate or declare mip levels.
.TP
.B \-\-encode <codec>
Encode to basis\-lz, uastc or a UASTC HDR codec; ASTC formats are encoded directly.
.TP
.B \-\-assign\-tf, \-\-convert\-tf, \-\-assign\-primaries, \-\-convert\-primaries
Color space handling.
.TP
.B \-\-zstd <level>, \-\-zlib <level>
Supercompress the result.
.TP
.B \-\-threads <n>
Number of encoder threads.
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
.nf
ktx create \-\-format R8G8B8A8_SRGB \-\-generate\-mipmap albedo.png albedo.ktx2
.fi
.PP
.nf
ktx create \-\-format ASTC_6x6_SRGB_BLOCK \-\-astc\-quality medium in.png out.ktx2
.fi
.SH NOTES
This is an unofficial Rust port of Khronos KTX\-Software (libktx and the ktx CLI); it is not
the Khronos build of the tool. The complete, current option list is printed by
.B ktx create \-\-help.
.SH SEE ALSO
ktx(1)
